# Shop / product archive: complete compact-card dataset

## Invariant

`/shop` and product archive routes intentionally ship a **complete compact product-card dataset** (prebuilt / SSR / ISR). Client filters and pagination must stay **instant** against that in-memory set.

## Do not

- On-demand card chunking or lazy card-data fetching after a filter
- Server-roundtrip filters / search that replace the local complete set
- Partial archive SSR that omits card records until interaction
- Any UX where cards disappear or load only after filter changes
- Skip or weaken full R2 incremental-cache upload/populate on production build
- Replace OpenNext deploy (`deploy` / `deploy:opennext` / WSL deploy script) with bare `wrangler deploy`

## Allowed

- Render only the **active page** in the DOM; keep images lazy / viewport-loaded
- Slim individual compact card fields; validate serialized-size budget
- Improve background regeneration, atomicity, or stale-while-revalidate (users keep the previous snapshot while regen runs)
- Image / media optimizations that do not change the complete-dataset UX

## Deploy

Every production build must run the OpenNext path that **fully populates** the R2 inc-cache. Do not remove that step.

Preflight (no deploy): `npm run release:check` / `npm run release:build:verify` — see `docs/runbooks/cloudflare-release-preflight.md`.

## Approval

Any proposal that changes this architecture needs **explicit user approval** before implementation.
